- All 12 first-improvement and all 12 best-improvement terminal certificates are complete. Each final pass evaluated every declared legal unilateral alternative and found zero strict guarded-`F` improvements.
- The bounded joint catalogues contained 8,864 unique configurations in total and were exactly exhausted. The selected joint configuration strictly improved boundary-0 `F` over its seed on 4/12 anchors; the seed itself remained eligible.
- Peak RSS was **2.525 GiB** (2,710,806,528 bytes), below 5 GB. One Python process ran at niceness 15; all six recorded BLAS/OpenMP-related thread controls were `1`.
- The interpreter was `/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python`. The read-only handover tree and its virtual environment were not modified. All generated files are under this workspace.
- Exact corpus provenance passed for configuration ID and complete default/incumbent mappings on 12/12 anchors. The corpus's dense nominal source call and the singleton nominal provenance check were numerically close at `1e-10` on 0/12 anchors and had equal served counts on 1/12. This is a verified evaluator batch-schedule sensitivity, so corpus-stored dense metrics were not substituted for the oracle's fixed singleton/microbatch schedule.
- A discarded diagnostic selected on nominal `G = F + kappa*Phi`; it is preserved only as `.scratch/panelceil/panelceil-nominal-G-diagnostic.json` and supplies no reported number here. The reportable run selects on realised boundary-0 `F`, matching the standing oracle construction.

